<h2>Segment 222 &mdash; the deed after cessation</h2>
<div class="pair">
<div class="tib"><div class="lab">TIBETAN (WYLIE)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s222S"><span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w1">las</span> de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w2">byas pa</span>&#x27;i <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w3">skad cig gnyis par</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w4">zhig</span> na <span class="u particle" data-d="6" data-l="s222w5">ni</span>, <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w6">mtshams de nas</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w7">&#x27;bras bu</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w8">dngos su</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w9">&#x27;byin pa</span>&#x27;i snga logs kyi bar du <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w10">las</span> de <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w11">med</span> la, <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w12">las</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w13">zhig pa</span> yang <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w14">dngos por</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w15">med</span> pas <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w16">las</span> las <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w17">&#x27;bras bu</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w18">ji ltar</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w19">&#x27;byung bar</span> &#x27;gyur zhes <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w20">brtsad pa</span>&#x27;i lan du</span>
</div>
<div class="eng"><div class="lab">GESHE MICHAEL'S ENGLISH (VERBATIM)</div>
<span class="u" data-d="1" data-l="s222S">From the <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w3">moment after</span> you <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w2">complete</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w1">karma or deed</span>, that deed is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w4">finished and gone</span>. During the entire period <span class="u" data-d="3" data-l="s222w6">from that point</span> up to the point at which the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w7">consequence</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w8">actually</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w9">occurs</span>, the <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w10">deed</span> <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w11">no longer exists</span>. A <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w12">deed</span> which is already <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w13">gone</span> is <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w15">no longer</span> a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w14">thing</span> that can have any affect on anything. <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w18">How</span> then does a <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w16">deed or karma</span> ever <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w19">produce</span> any kind of <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w17">consequence</span>? Here is how we explain this <span class="u" data-d="5" data-l="s222w20">problem</span>:<span class="u" data-d="6" data-l="s222w5"><span class="nul">Topic particle has no separate English exponent.</span></span></span>
</div>
</div>
<div class="note"><b>AI NOTE</b> &mdash; Provisional machine alignment by Codex, Tibetan-first independent proposal. Initial las owns karma or deed once; the later that deed repeats this participant and remains unwrapped. The second and third Tibetan las attach to deed after occurs and deed before which respectively, as proved by occurrence offsets. skad cig gnyis par is the second instant recast as moment after, retained at phrase depth; gnyis par alone is not banked as after. zhig/zhig pa are cessation verbs here, not indefinite particles; misleading short HGM headword entries are not imported. ILL:1878 supplies a shorter Tibetan parallel with a different English rendering that supports the shared cessation/functioning reading only through brtsad pa'i. dngos por owns thing; the English explanation that can have any affect on anything stays unwrapped. The two med occurrences own no longer exists and no longer respectively. Temporal snga logs kyi bar du and final lan du are distributed recasts and omitted rather than falsely nulled. Supplied participants, articles and auxiliary frames remain unaligned.</div>
